Replace $x$ with $x/3$ and $y$ with $y/2$.

$\begin{aligned}\left(\frac{x}{3}\right)^2+\left(\frac{y}{2}\right)^2&=4\\\frac{x^2}{9}+\frac{y^2}{4}&=4\\\frac{x^2}{36}+\frac{y^2}{16}&=1\end{aligned}$

The original intercepts $(\pm2,0)$ and $(0,\pm2)$ become $(\pm6,0)$ and $(0,\pm4)$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{dilationBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,->] (-7,0)--(7,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,-5)--(0,5);
\path (7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\path (0,5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dilationBlue,thick] (0,0) ellipse [x radius=30mm,y radius=20mm];
\fill[dilationBlue] (-6,0) circle[radius=0.6mm];
\fill[dilationBlue] (6,0) circle[radius=0.6mm];
\fill[dilationBlue] (0,4) circle[radius=0.6mm];
\fill[dilationBlue] (0,-4) circle[radius=0.6mm];
\path (-6,0) node[below left] {$(-6,0)$};
\path (6,0) node[below right] {$(6,0)$};
\path (0,4) node[above right] {$(0,4)$};
\path (0,-4) node[below right] {$(0,-4)$};
